<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!-- P3-7: the dashboard groups `transactions` by a `created_at` range and nothing else.

         None of the three indexes from 007 serves that. `idx_transactions_status_created` leads
         with `status`, and the summary filters no status — it counts all six. A leading column
         that is not in the predicate cannot be used for the range, so every dashboard load would
         read the whole table, and `transactions` is the fastest-growing table in the system: one
         row per payment attempt, forever.

         This was decided by reasoning, not by EXPLAIN: there is no installation with production
         volumes to measure on, and on a development database every plan is a sequential scan and
         every plan is fast. Recorded here so that the *presence* of this index reads as a
         decision, the same way SearchTerms records the absence of pg_trgm.

         Not composite: the company scope lives on `payment_links.terminal_id`, one join away, and
         `idx_payment_links_term_status` from 002 already leads with that column. Adding columns
         here that the predicate cannot reach would cost insert time and buy nothing.

         One index per changeset behind its own precondition, for the reason stated in 002: a
         database restored from a dump without its DATABASECHANGELOG must skip what is already
         there and still create what is missing. The changeset id carries the module name — all
         three services share one DATABASECHANGELOG table (problems.md). -->

    <changeSet id="8-pbl-index-transactions-created" author="millikart">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN">
            <not>
                <indexExists tableName="transactions" indexName="idx_transactions_created"/>
            </not>
        </preConditions>
        <createIndex tableName="transactions" indexName="idx_transactions_created"><column name="created_at"/></createIndex>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
